---
// Thermite's three campaign modes, each with a small drawing of what it does.
---

<div class="grid three modes">
  <a class="card" href="/explanation/campaign-modes/">
    <svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 220 90" aria-hidden="true">
      <path class="grid-l" d="M10 80H210M10 55H210M10 30H210"></path>
      <path class="dash" d="M10 34H210"></path>
      <path class="area" d="M10 74H52V66H78V54H104V47H126V40H150V33H176V27H210V80H10Z"></path>
      <path class="line" d="M10 74H52V66H78V54H104V47H126V40H150V33H176V27H210"></path>
      <circle class="dot gold" cx="52" cy="66" r="3"></circle><circle class="dot gold" cx="104" cy="47" r="3"></circle><circle class="dot gold" cx="176" cy="27" r="3"></circle>
      <circle class="dot slow" cx="66" cy="76" r="2.4"></circle><circle class="dot slow" cx="118" cy="60" r="2.4"></circle><circle class="dot flat" cx="140" cy="41" r="2.4"></circle><circle class="dot flat" cx="190" cy="28" r="2.4"></circle>
    </svg>
    <span class="tag climb">hill climb</span>
    <h3 class="h3">Make it faster</h3>
    <p>
      Push one number as far as it will go: speed, size, accuracy, a score. Guards hold everything else where it
      started. It runs until you stop it.
    </p>
    <p class="eg">For example: tokens a second on your GPU.</p>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="/explanation/campaign-modes/">
    <svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 220 90" aria-hidden="true">
      <g class="check on"><rect x="14" y="10" width="16" height="16" rx="4"></rect><path d="M18 18l3.5 3.5L27 14"></path></g>
      <rect class="bar on" x="40" y="15" width="120" height="6" rx="3"></rect>
      <g class="check on"><rect x="14" y="37" width="16" height="16" rx="4"></rect><path d="M18 45l3.5 3.5L27 41"></path></g>
      <rect class="bar on" x="40" y="42" width="92" height="6" rx="3"></rect>
      <g class="check"><rect x="14" y="64" width="16" height="16" rx="4"></rect></g>
      <rect class="bar" x="40" y="69" width="140" height="6" rx="3"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span class="tag goal">goal</span>
    <h3 class="h3">Make it work</h3>
    <p>
      List what the result must do, as checks: it builds, it loads the model, its answers match. Agents work
      until every goal passes, or the evidence shows it can't.
    </p>
    <p class="eg">For example: support a new quantized format.</p>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="/explanation/campaign-modes/">
    <svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 220 90" aria-hidden="true">
      <rect class="page" x="10" y="8" width="120" height="74" rx="6"></rect>
      <rect class="bar" x="22" y="22" width="90" height="5" rx="2.5"></rect>
      <rect class="quote" x="22" y="35" width="78" height="5" rx="2.5"></rect>
      <rect class="bar" x="22" y="48" width="96" height="5" rx="2.5"></rect>
      <rect class="bar" x="22" y="61" width="60" height="5" rx="2.5"></rect>
      <path class="link" d="M100 37C130 37 140 45 156 45"></path>
      <rect class="claim" x="156" y="30" width="56" height="30" rx="6"></rect>
      <path class="tick" d="M172 45l5 5 10-10"></path>
    </svg>
    <span class="tag research">research</span>
    <h3 class="h3">Find out</h3>
    <p>
      Ask a question. Agents read sources and record claims, and code finds every quote, word for word, in the
      page it came from. You get a report built on checked sources.
    </p>
    <p class="eg">For example: which papers improve 2-bit decoding?</p>
  </a>
</div>

<style>
  .art {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .grid-l {
    stroke: var(--rule-2);
    stroke-width: 1;
    fill: none;
  }
  .dash {
    stroke: var(--dim);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 4;
    fill: none;
  }
  .area {
    fill: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .dot.gold {
    fill: var(--gold);
  }
  .dot.slow {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, var(--dim));
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .dot.flat {
    fill: var(--dim);
  }
  .check rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--rule-2);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  .check.on rect {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 16%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--teal);
  }
  .check path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--teal);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .bar {
    fill: var(--rule-2);
  }
  .bar.on {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 45%, var(--rule-2));
  }
  .page {
    fill: var(--panel);
    stroke: var(--rule-2);
  }
  .quote {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--gold) 60%, transparent);
  }
  .link {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--gold);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }
  .claim {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--gold) 12%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--gold);
  }
  .tick {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--gold);
    stroke-width: 2.2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .h3 {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
  }
  .eg {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--dim) !important;
  }
</style>
